sourceAuthoredSummary:
The following changes were made:
-	Editorial changes, e.g. italicized field values, inconsistencies in field names between ASN.1 and procedural text, etc.;
-	Introducing a new list for reporting logged data for network-side data collection to avoid repeating the logging configuration ID for every measurement entry;
-	Changing some fields in ASN.1 from optional to mandatory;
-	Changing some field names for clarity;
-	Rephrasing some procedural text for clarity, better alignment with legacy cases, and better alignment with draft capability descriptions;
-	Some modifications to the ASN.1 content and structure of the event-triggered CSI logging configuration and of the parameters for prediction, UE-side data collection and monitoring within CSI-ReportConfig;
-	Introducing a new IE in HandoverPreparationInformation message to convey applicability information;
-	Introducing a new flag to disable applicability reports for beam management prediction configurations in CSI-ReportConfig;
-	Clarifying in the procedural text that a periodic CSI report configuration for prediction is submitted to the lower layers only if it is reported by the UE as applicable in RRCReconfigurationComplete
-	Removing the definition of “Applicable AI/ML configuration”;
-	Renumbering clause “5.5a Logged Measurements for Network-Side Data Collection” (and the subclauses within) as “5.5c Logged Measurements for Network-Side Data Collection”.

